{
  "understanding": "The supplied code partially recovers a Raft library with separate candidate, commitment, FSM, and snapshot responsibilities. Observed mechanisms include voter-index aggregation, candidate vote tallying, asynchronous client admission, optional batched application, snapshot capture and compaction, and startup snapshot restoration. Documentation and interface comments describe stronger contracts than the inspected fragments alone establish. Replication acknowledgement production, configuration activation, leader dispatch, startup adapter selection, and several storage error paths remain unread. No correctness, calibration, or reproduction conclusion is established.",
  "audit_spec": {
    "version": 1,
    "target_profile": {
      "system_boundary": "The repository's Raft coordination, application scheduling, recovery orchestration, and built-in storage and transport implementations are within the descriptive audit boundary. Client FSM semantics and separately maintained storage implementations are external implementations. Their integration contracts remain relevant.",
      "protocol_contexts": [
        "Raft roles and election terms, with optional pre-voting and a leadership-transfer election path.",
        "Protocol-version-dependent RPC compatibility and membership representation.",
        "Leader commitment tracking over a mutable voter-ID map.",
        "Asynchronous FSM application and snapshot capture, persistence, restoration, and log compaction."
      ],
      "external_interfaces": [
        "Apply, ApplyLog, Barrier, and VerifyLeader return futures.",
        "Transport exposes RPC delivery, replication pipelines, vote requests, snapshot streaming, heartbeat callbacks, and TimeoutNow; WithPreVote is optional.",
        "FSM, BatchingFSM, and FSMSnapshot are client implementation interfaces.",
        "Snapshot store, log store, and stable store integration is visible through calls and documentation; full interface contracts are not yet inspected."
      ],
      "ownership": [
        "runCandidate handles candidate-state events in the main Raft execution loop.",
        "commitment serializes voter progress and commit-index calculations with a mutex.",
        "runFSM owns local application progress and invokes client callbacks.",
        "takeSnapshot requests FSM capture and separately requests main-thread-owned configuration state.",
        "FileSnapshotSink owns buffered snapshot output and filesystem publication steps."
      ],
      "selection_injection": [
        "runFSM detects BatchingFSM and ConfigurationStore by interface assertions on r.fsm.",
        "Transport allows either an optional heartbeat fast path or normal Consumer delivery.",
        "Constructor selection of storage, transport, and FSM adapters is unread; currently activated variants are unknown.",
        "The supplied FileSnapshotSink code is a built-in implementation and remains in scope despite unknown activation.",
        "README identifies separately maintained MDB and Bbolt backends; their implementations are outside the supplied repository materials."
      ],
      "variants": [
        "Pre-vote enabled versus disabled; leadership transfer bypasses pre-vote.",
        "Single-entry FSM application versus BatchingFSM.",
        "Optional ConfigurationStore callback.",
        "Startup snapshot restoration versus NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart.",
        "Versioned snapshot configuration versus legacy peer decoding.",
        "File snapshot synchronization enabled versus noSync; parent-directory synchronization is skipped on Windows.",
        "Legacy and newer membership log representations are described in config.go; active protocol version is unknown."
      ],
